# rac-rs architecture

Map of the engine source: where things live and what a change will touch. Written 2026-10-21 after the five giant files
were split by job. Companion files: `STATE.md` (global mutable state and threads), `ENV.md` (every environment switch, kept
honest by `src/env_doc_tests.rs`), `SIZE_CAPS.txt` (the files and fns still over the size limits, kept by
`src/size_limits_tests.rs`), `CLAUDE.md` (build, run, keys). Comment tags in the code: **[C]** read in code or data,
**[I]** inferred, **[?]** unknown. Notes on retail facts live outside the repo in `D:\ratchet\decomp\notes\` (comments cite them).

## 1. What the engine is

- rac-rs is the PC half of the Ratchet & Clank 1 port (PAL and USA v1.00). It reads everything from the player's own disc at run time.
- The game logic is the retail PS2 code, recompiled from the disc and run by ee-oracle / ee-game (`D:\ratchet\oracle`, not in this repo). Retail mode is the only game path.
- Speed hands (dev s93): ee-oracle runs 11 of the hottest retail functions as exact native Rust (`oracle/src/hs_hands/`, installed by `rec::Table::build` where the code words match; same RAM and timing; RAC_HS=0 = off). rac-rs only prints their report after `smoke: done` (`retail/debug_aids.rs`).
- rac-rs gives that code the pad once per field, reads the game's RAM back (mobys, camera, lights, GS packets, sound) and draws it with a native wgpu renderer plus PC extras.
- The crate is the library `rac_game` (`src/lib.rs` includes `src/main.rs`); the exe in `exe/` links it with the recompiled crates.
- A field is one retail step (50 Hz PAL, about 60 Hz USA). The viewer calls the same thing a tick.

Threads (details and owners: `STATE.md`):

- MAIN: winit loop, `handler` frame steps, wgpu render, `Retail::tick`, level switch.
- retail worker ("retail", 256 MB stack): EE interpreter plus recompiled code, PC hooks, snapshot build (`retail/worker/`).
- GS capture ("gs-relay", "gs", rayon "gs-capture-N", "gs-gpu-open"): draws the HUD and menu packets (`retail/capture.rs`, `retail/gscap*`).
- "snap", "snap-prep" and "vu1": the effects layer's picture work (`retail/snap_pipe.rs`, `retail/efx_vu.rs`).
- GS-full ("gsfull-vu1", "gsfull-gs", "gs-raster-N"): optional full software GS (`gsfull/`).
- "level-prefetch" (64 MB stack) builds the next level during travel; "level-drop" frees the old one (`viewer/app.rs`).
- "present" and "enc-finish-N": wgpu submit and present, command-buffer finish (`viewer/presenter.rs`).
- audio callback (cpal, `audio.rs`), "fmv decode" (`fmv/player.rs`), "pspad" and "xinput search" (`retail/pspad.rs`, `retail/prompts.rs`), "veg plan" (`viewer/vegfx.rs`), log writer (`loadlog.rs`), "runlog" watchdog (`runlog.rs`, the player's log.txt).

One frame (the worker runs up to 3 fields ahead; `RAC_RUN_AHEAD=0` turns that off):

```
keys / mouse / pad (winit events in viewer/handler.rs window_event, play_input.rs)
   |
   v  frame_input, frame_ticks -> Retail::tick_keys (retail/input.rs) -> Retail::tick (retail/tick.rs)
FieldIn { buttons, sticks, travel, mc }  ---- mpsc ---->  retail worker: worker_main (retail/worker/spawn.rs)
                                                          field_begin -> field_ee (EE runs the field) -> field_front
                                                          -> field_load_loop -> field_post -> field_capture_end
                                                          -> field_snap -> field_levels -> field_overlay -> field_end
Snap (mobys, camera, lights, fx, shadows,   <---- mpsc ----   (GS packets go to the capture thread, effects to snap / vu1,
      sound batch, overlay)                                    sound batch to Retail::take_sound)
   |
   v  MAIN: RedrawRequested = 20 steps in viewer/handler.rs (files in viewer/handler/):
frame_begin, frame_input, frame_ticks, frame_shadows, frame_sound_events, frame_camera, frame_hero, frame_hero_scene,
frame_hero_fx, frame_props, frame_hud_state, frame_hud_draw, frame_upload, frame_cam_restore, frame_audio_events,
frame_audio_anim, frame_audio_music, frame_audio_ambience, frame_switch, frame_render
   |
   v  frame_render -> Gpu::draw (viewer/gpu/draw.rs) -> present (viewer/presenter.rs thread)
frame_uniforms, frame_effects, frame_target, frame_buffers (viewer/gpu/draw/prepare.rs)
draw_passes (draw/passes.rs, owns every render-pass begin and drop):
   pass_sky, pass_world (with pass_pools, pass_shrubs), pass_oceans, pass_world_quads, pass_shop_models,
   particle_runs + particle_buffers (particle passes), post chain (viewer/post.rs), pass_hud, pass_previews
frame_finish (draw/finish.rs: movie overlay, readback, submit)
```

Retail mode: `Retail::load` (`retail/worker.rs`) is a list of steps in `retail/worker/` (open_machine, register_hooks, begin_rec,
first_snapshot, gs_setup, travel_request, open_feeds, spawn_worker). `viewer/handler/frame_switch.rs` keeps the `Retail`
across a level switch (`retail_carry`); `Retail::switch` (`retail/props_sync.rs`) rebinds the prop pools.

## 2. Module map

Each table is generated from the files' own `//!` headers (script: `D:\ratchet\scratch_perf_rf\docs_draft\build_arch.py`). Lines = file length.
Split pattern: a parent file is the front door (types, `mod` list, re-exports); each child starts with `use super::*;`, so old paths such as `retail::x` still work.

