| `omni/pose.rs`, `pose_host.rs`, `pose_read.rs`, `pose_capture.rs`, `pose_tests.rs`, `pose_read_tests.rs`, `pose_capture_tests.rs`, `viewer/handler/pose_service.rs` | ABI 1.4 pose overrides of the hero (`openrac.omni.pose`: `pose_set` / `pose_info` / `pose_read` / `pose_snapshot` / `pose_debug`; host size 352, a 1.3 DLL still gets 312). RENDER-ONLY: nothing writes game RAM. `pose.rs` = the store (ops per (moby, joint): mirror / set / offset rotation / hold, weight ramps by `blend_ticks`, `duration_ticks`, `remove` and `n = 0` fade out, cap 64, errors -3/-4/-5) and the auto-clear rules run by `pose::tick` from `omni::tick` (level change, level-loop exit, game modes 1/2/5, hero death states fade, other mobys dropped; also drops snapshots and the read cache) and `clear_all()` on `new_game` / `save_loaded` in `events.rs send`; `snapshot_for` turns the ops into `JointFx` records for `HeroParts.pose_ops` (`retail/snapshot.rs snap`; applied by `Animated::local_fx_parts` / `anim_pose.rs`). `pose_host.rs` = the five callbacks (only the hero cell's class-0, 111-joint moby is posable), the parent / partner tables (bone table + the binding's `skeletons.hero` pairs) and `debug_tick`. `pose_read.rs` = `pose_read`, PURE reads (no retail call, `&Cpu` only, nothing written): the nine hero attach matrices retail writes each tick at `0x13fe10` (right hand / weapon grip = matrix 0; joints 56 55 99 93 7 5 54 3 5; current tick; same data layout on PAL and USA) and every other joint (left hand, chest, fingers) from the last rendered pose slot, ONE FRAME BEHIND the tick (render-timing dependent: for looks only); one copy of the slot per tick (`new_tick`); `flags` bit 0 = reflection across the chest plane (normal = the hero moby's left axis from RAM, offset = the chest's lateral distance from the slot, 0 before the first frame). `pose_capture.rs` = the "last rendered hero pose" slot: `pose_snapshot` (and a `hold` with no snapshot) registers a request and returns its id, `viewer/handler/pose_service.rs` (once per frame, three atomic loads when idle) captures the base local rotations of the hero (retail records + leg twist, no pose ops) and fulfils it, a hold becomes a rotation SET at the captured rotation (effective one frame later); while a mod reads joints (`pose_read`, `reads_on`) the service publishes the world frame of every joint of the game pose (`publish_world`); while `pose_debug` is on it publishes the world position of every drawn joint and the worker projects them with the game camera into a dot + name draw list (`draw.rs submit_debug`, drawn after the mods' list by `pass_omni`). Tests: store, binding section, partner cross-check vs `Animated::partner_table`, savestates, reflect, capture / hold / debug / reads, pure reads vs the recorded retail-call values. | 353 + 145 + 171 + 203 + 61 + 245 + 264 + 159 |
| `omni/pose_follow.rs`, `pose_follow_tests.rs` | ABI 1.6 `pose_follow` (`openrac.omni.pose.follow`): picture-only follow poses. HOST STORE (up to 8 records item/source/from/to/mirror, same auto-clear as pose ops plus drop when the item or source slot holds another moby: `Store::run_rules`), the callback (`pose_follow_cb`: remove always 0; -1 no level, -2 hero not posable, -3 bad joint, -7 not a live moby, -8 cap) and `snapshot_for`, which reaches the renderer as `HeroParts.follow` (retail/snapshot.rs `mod_poses`). Never writes RAM. The picture side is `viewer/follow.rs`. | 178 + 66 |
