## 3. Where to change X

| Task | Files |
|---|---|
| Speed hand (exact native rewrite of a hot retail function) | not in rac-rs: `oracle/src/hs_hands/` (generated in lane `scratch_perf_hs`, see its PLAN.md; no new hands unless the user asks) |
| Renderer (Vulkan / DirectX 12), RivaTuner layer, DXC | `viewer/gpu/renderer.rs` (backend, compiler, latency), `retail/pcrender.rs` + the Renderer row in `retail/pcctl.rs` / `retail/pcext.rs`, `rtss_layer.rs`; setup.ps1 fetches `dxcompiler.dll` (`Install-Dxc`) |
| Mod loader / mod hooks (OmniLoader host, Luau mods) | `src/omni/*`: new hook point = a line `hook <id>` + spec in `omni/rac1_reloc.txt` (made by `scratch_perf_omni/tools/make_reloc_data.py` from `hsreloc.py spec`) + its entry in the `hooks` array of `omni/rac1.json`, no code change below 256 hooks (`MAX_HOOKS` and the `tables!` list in `omni/hooks.rs`); a PC feature a mod can replace = a `Feature` row in `omni/clash.rs` and a `&& !clash::off(ID)` term at its gate; new host entry = `omni/host.rs` (or its own file, as `omni/input_host.rs`) + `omni/cabi.rs` (ABI 1.2: host size 296, optional exports `omni_event` / `omni_storage_dir` / `omni_set_setting` / `omni_settings_json`); new mod event = a variant in `omni/events.rs`; mouse / keyboard / pointer for mods = `omni/input.rs` (feeds in `viewer/handler.rs`, the per-field snapshot in `retail/tick.rs` and `retail/worker/field_run.rs`) |
| New PC Options row (Pause -> Options) | `retail/pcext.rs` (rows, `patch_graphics`), `retail/pcopts.rs` (file key), `retail/pcctl.rs` (Controls page); a Camera Options row: a new file next to `retail/pcext/mousespeed.rs`, its record in `pcext.rs` `patch_rows_at` (table `TAB`, 9 records at BASE+0x1200, inside the camopts block) |
| Camera speed / Mouse speed (Camera Options rows, `camspeed=` / `mousespeed=`) | stick: `retail/pcext/camopts.rs` (`camspeed_scale`); mouse: `retail/pcext/mousespeed.rs` (`mousespeed_scale`); both read by `retail/modcam.rs` `step` through `retail/modcam_turn.rs` (`turn`, `Gains`); keys: `retail/pcopts.rs` |
| Which way the right stick / mouse turns the Modern camera (Normal / Reversed) | `retail/modcam_turn.rs` (`stick_axes`, `turn`); the keys' share of the stick travels as `Retail.kb_rs` (`retail/input.rs` `tick_keys`) -> `FieldIn.mc.keys` (`retail/tick.rs`) -> `modcam::Input.keys`, recorded by `retail/rec.rs` |
| New Graphics quality level | `retail/pcext.rs` (`Graphics`, `pack_gfx`), `retail/pcopts.rs` (`draw_level`), `viewer/gpu/draw/prepare.rs` (`frame_effects`), then the effect file |
| Graphics presets (Low / Medium / High values, the Preset row) | the table is ONE file, `assets/gfx_presets.txt` (the launcher's `ui/presets.rs` TABLE must equal it: a test compares them when the launcher sources are next to the project); the row is `retail/pcext/presets.rs` (`choose`, `show`) and `retail/pcctl.rs` (`PRESETB`, `preset_chosen`, `preset_show`, `gfx_table`); a new picture option = a key in the file for all three presets |
| Mods page (Pause / title -> Options -> Mods), `mods/active.txt`, `mods/settings.json`; when the Mods row is in the Options list | `retail/pcmods.rs` (pages, rows, `sync`, `front_field`, `load_store` = the pause row's rule), `omni/modset.rs` (a setting -> menu row: bool / choice 2-4 / int,float as <=4 values; advanced, string, keybind: launcher only), `omni/plugins.rs` (active.txt + settings.json -> the loader's plugins list; settings.json read / one-key write), `omni/live_settings.rs` (a pause change reaches the running mod at once: `omni_set_setting`), `texpack/store.rs` (installed packs + script mods by manifest id + file), `texpack/active.rs` (the launcher's file format; fixtures `texpack/fixtures/launcher_*.txt`), `texpack/mod.rs` (`refresh`: the packs rebuild at a planet load when the file changed), `retail/pcext.rs` (`patch_graphics` row, `build_title`, `text_hook`), `viewer/front_mirror.rs` + `frontend.rs` (the title page's drawing) |
| Water look, waves | `viewer/waterfx/shader.rs`, `looks.rs` (`wave_look`, `march_steps`), `levels.rs`, `passes.rs` |
| Waterfall, rings, wakes | `viewer/waterfx/fall_sheets.rs`, `contacts.rs`, `wakes.rs` |
| Water mirror, underwater | `viewer/mirror.rs`, `viewer/underwater.rs`, `viewer/gpu/draw.rs` (`mirror_pick`) |
| Oceans, sky | `viewer/gpu/sky_water.rs`, `viewer/gpu/draw/pass_world.rs` (`pass_sky`), `pass_water.rs` (`pass_oceans`), `ocean.rs`, `sky.rs` |
| Vegetation | `viewer/vegfx.rs`, `viewer/gpu/draw/pass_shrubs.rs`, `viewer/gpu/culling.rs` (`cull_shrubs`), `shrubs.rs` |
| `viewer/volfog.rs` | Graphics -> Fog row Low / Medium / High (with Lighting Enhanced): volumetric fog pass (march, temporal accumulation, depth-aware apply) after the water pass; no retail counterpart; Classic draws the retail fog alone. | 375 |
| `viewer/volfog/density.rs` | Fog: how thick the air is at a world point (height fog, drifting wisps, Kerwan sheet volume) and how the level's retail fog sets the amount. | 93 |
| `viewer/volfog/frame.rs` | Fog: the per-frame inputs (level, retail fog, light colour, sheet height) and the RAC_FOG_LOG log. | 102 |
| `viewer/volfog/gputime.rs` | Fog: GPU timestamp queries around the three passes (RAC_FOG_LOG=1 prints ms per pass). | 83 |
| `viewer/volfog/noise.rs` | Shared by fog and clouds: the tiling 3D noise volume (CPU generated, 64^3). | 134 |
| `viewer/volfog/scatter.rs` | Shared by fog and clouds: uniform block, sun phase, sun shadow visibility, jittered ray march WGSL. | 142 |
| `viewer/volfog/temporal.rs` | Shared by fog and clouds: reprojection and neighbourhood-clamped temporal accumulation WGSL. | 44 |
| `viewer/volfog/tests.rs` | Unit tests of the volumetric fog pass (shader parse, uniform size, quality levels). | 28 |
| `viewer/volclouds.rs` | Graphics -> Effects -> Volumetric clouds Low / Medium / High (with Lighting Enhanced): a cloud slab in the world ray-marched on a coarse grid with volfog's noise / scatter / temporal tools, accumulated and laid over the sky (and anything behind the layer) before the fog pass; `sky_skip` = the retail sky shell draws it replaces; no retail counterpart. | 273 |
| `viewer/volclouds/input.rs` | Clouds: the per-frame inputs (level, picture size, light and fog colours, direction to the key light) and `level` (RAC_TUNE cl_q override). | 68 |
| `viewer/volclouds/layer.rs` | Clouds: the WGSL of the cloud medium (weather map, height profile, erosion, sun march, multi-scatter, Beer-Powder) and the march / apply entry points. | 178 |
| `viewer/volclouds/params.rs` | Clouds: quality levels, per-level look (coverage, altitude, none on space and dark levels), sun direction floor, ambient colour, slab altitudes, retail sky shell mask. | 93 |
| `viewer/volclouds/tests.rs` | Unit tests of the cloud pass (shader parse, uniform size, quality levels, sun floor). | 47 |
