| Gate test switches (fixed clock) | `viewer/test_clock.rs` |
| New feature or new job | a new file (module) next to the related ones, with its `//!` header and a line in the parent's map; never append it to the biggest nearby file |
| A file or fn grew too big | split the file into modules by job (pure move, `movecheck.py`) or break the fn into named steps (`FUNC_RULES.md`); `src/size_limits_tests.rs` fails until then |
| New env switch | read it in code, add a row to `ENV.md`; `src/env_doc_tests.rs` fails without it |
| New global (static, thread_local) | add a row to `STATE.md` |
| New gate scene | `D:\ratchet\gate\cases.txt`, steps in `D:\ratchet\gate\README.md` ("Adding a case") |
| New unit test | beside the code, or `retail/test_suite.rs`, `viewer/gpu/tests.rs` |

## 4. State and switches

- `STATE.md` lists every static, thread_local and set-once value with writer, reader, thread and lifetime, plus the thread table.
- Counts: retail 116 items (37 Mutex, 73 Atomic, 6 thread_local), viewer 51, audio 11, gsfull and others about 30, 79 read-only OnceLocks.
- Top risks: level-prefetch writes `mobies::MIP_KS` and `gpu::MOBY_CHAINS` with no deferral; `Drop for Retail` does not join the worker; many retail statics have no reset at `Retail::load`.
- Also: PC options live in four places (kept in step only by `pcext::sync`); `session::STATE/COLD/START_LEVEL` are set-once.
- `ENV.md` lists every `RAC_*` switch (about 240 rows) by category: player, harness, debug, tune, kill, dead?.
- A new static or env switch needs its row in the same change.

## 5. Safe-change rules

- One lane per file area (a lane owns a file and its directory). Never edit a file another lane owns.
- Pure moves are proven by `python -B D:\ratchet\scratch_perf_rf\tools\movecheck.py --new <lane>/rac-rs/src <F>.rs <F>`; it must end with `PURE MOVE`.
- Breaking up a function follows `D:\ratchet\scratch_perf_rf\FUNC_RULES.md`: contiguous steps, same order, early exits kept, no behaviour change.
- Every new file starts with a `//!` header (its job, 1-4 lines); a parent keeps the `//!` map of its children. Keep both honest.
- Size limits (2026-10-22, `src/size_limits_tests.rs`): a hand-written file at most 1500 lines, a fn at most 150 lines (rac-rs src and exe/src, oracle src, core/src, game/src; files with a "generated by" header line are exempt). The ones over on 2026-10-22 have a cap in `SIZE_CAPS.txt` (11 files, 51 fns) that only goes down: growing fails, shrinking fails until `RAC_SIZE_CAPS_WRITE=1 cargo test --lib size_limits` lowers the cap, and a raised or added cap fails against git HEAD. A new feature goes in a new file.
- Every merge runs the gate (`D:\ratchet\gate\gate.ps1 -Exe <exe> -Tag <tag> -Jobs 6`, deterministic with `RAC_TEST_CLOCK=1`, RAM hashes plus pictures vs approved references; see `D:\ratchet\gate\README.md`) and the unit tests (the size limits among them).
- Unit test baseline (2026-10-22): 482 passed, 1 failed (`hud::tests::fonts_decode`: its output folder target\test_out\hud is missing), 22 ignored. On a fresh target folder `fmv::mpeg2::tests::decode_movie_one` and `gadgets::tests::wrench_textures` fail too until a test has made target\test_out. `retail::pcext::camopts_tests` can flake in parallel.
- Match retail exactly by default. PC extras sit behind the Options menu, are tagged `[PC]` in headers, and must leave the RAM hashes untouched when off.
- Files are LF, ASCII, tab-indented, no BOM unless the file already has one. Do not `sed -i` a CRLF file.

## 6. Running and building

- Entry: no arguments = the player start (reads `generated/play.cfg` written by Setup, asks about updates, cold boot with the modern camera). With arguments: `rac-rs view ISO LEVEL --retail STATE_DIR` (savestate) or `--retail-cold` (boot from the disc); other flags: `--title`, `--shot out.png`, `--cam x y z yaw pitch`, `--give ITEM`, `--gsfull`, `--wide`, `--modern-cam`. `view` without `--retail` or `--retail-cold` is an error. Other commands: `levels`, `terrain`, `ties`, `scan`, `verify`, `dump`.
- Build: `cargo build --release --target-dir D:/ratchet/scratch_NAME` (the flag, not the env var, so sccache works; `timeout 600`). The 458-crate ee-game build needs an empty `RUSTC_WRAPPER`. Lane builds: `D:\ratchet\scratch_perf_tools\build.ps1 -Lane NAME`.
- Tests: `cargo test --release` (most read the disc at `D:\ratchet\Ratchet & Clank (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It) (v1.00).iso`); retail savestate probes are `#[ignore]`.
- Keys and env vars for play and tests: `CLAUDE.md`, `ENV.md`.
- Units: 1024 = 1.0 fixed point, metres, Z up; PAL steps of 0.02 s.
- Dependencies (`Cargo.toml`): wgpu 30, winit 0.30, cpal, rayon, bytemuck, pollster, ee-oracle (path).
